@ops = http://localhost:4004/operations
@bill = http://localhost:4004/billing
@vc1 = d1000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001
@sept = d2000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001
@manual = 92000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001

### ── A) Rules 1 + 2 ──

### 1) Should FAIL 409: VC-2026-0002 is PLANNED, not DEPARTED
POST {{bill}}/VesselCalls(d1000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000002)/BillingService.generateInvoice
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### 2) VC-2026-0001 (WORKING) completes …
POST {{ops}}/VesselCalls({{vc1}})/OperationsService.complete
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### 3) … and departs
POST {{ops}}/VesselCalls({{vc1}})/OperationsService.depart
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### 4) Should FAIL 409: it already has the draft INV-2026-0002
POST {{bill}}/VesselCalls({{vc1}})/BillingService.generateInvoice
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### 5) Cancel INV-2026-0002
POST {{bill}}/Invoices(91000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000002)/BillingService.cancelInvoice
Content-Type: application/json

{ "reason": "Replaced by system-generated invoice" }

### 6) Generate → INV-2026-0003 with the lines calculated from the operational data
POST {{bill}}/VesselCalls({{vc1}})/BillingService.generateInvoice
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### 7) Look at its lines
GET {{bill}}/Invoices?$filter=invoiceNumber eq 'INV-2026-0003'&$select=invoiceNumber,status_code,netAmount,taxAmount,grossAmount,dueDate&$expand=items($select=lineNo,chargeType_code,description,quantity,unit,rate,amount)

### ── B) Rule 3: a visit in SEPTEMBER is priced with the OLD tariff ──

### 8) Create a call for KOCHI EXPRESS in September with a berth at B05
POST {{ops}}/VesselCalls
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "ID": "{{sept}}",
  "vessel_ID": "c1000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000005",
  "voyageNumber": "KX07",
  "shippingLine_ID": "b1000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000002",
  "agent_ID": "b1000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000003",
  "eta": "2026-09-10T06:00:00Z",
  "etd": "2026-09-11T08:00:00Z",
  "berthAllocations": [
    { "berth_ID": "a1000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000005", "fromTime": "2026-09-10T06:00:00Z", "toTime": "2026-09-11T08:00:00Z" }
  ]
}

### 9) Arrived 10 Sep 06:00
POST {{ops}}/VesselCalls({{sept}})/OperationsService.arrive
Content-Type: application/json

{ "ata": "2026-09-10T06:00:00Z" }

### 10) Berth
POST {{ops}}/VesselCalls({{sept}})/OperationsService.berth
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### 11) Start work
POST {{ops}}/VesselCalls({{sept}})/OperationsService.startWork
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### 12) Complete
POST {{ops}}/VesselCalls({{sept}})/OperationsService.complete
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### 13) Departed 11 Sep 08:00
POST {{ops}}/VesselCalls({{sept}})/OperationsService.depart
Content-Type: application/json

{ "atd": "2026-09-11T08:00:00Z" }

### 14) Generate its invoice
POST {{bill}}/VesselCalls({{sept}})/BillingService.generateInvoice
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### 15) Check: port dues rate 25.00 (old tariff), berth hire 26 h
GET {{bill}}/Invoices?$filter=call_ID eq {{sept}}&$select=invoiceNumber,netAmount,taxAmount,grossAmount&$expand=items($select=chargeType_code,quantity,rate,amount,tariff_ID)

### ── C) Rules 4 + 5: draft-only edits and automatic netAmount ──

### 16) Manual invoice with one item – the netAmount we send (1) is ignored
POST {{bill}}/Invoices
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "ID": "{{manual}}",
  "call_ID": "d1000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000003",
  "billTo_ID": "b1000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001",
  "invoiceDate": "2026-11-16",
  "currency_code": "INR",
  "netAmount": 1,
  "items": [
    { "ID": "02000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001", "lineNo": 1, "chargeType_code": "GATE_FEE", "quantity": 2, "rate": 600 }
  ]
}

### 17) Add an item → netAmount follows
POST {{bill}}/InvoiceItems
Content-Type: application/json

{ "ID": "02000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000002", "invoice_ID": "{{manual}}", "lineNo": 2, "chargeType_code": "DOC_FEE", "quantity": 1, "rate": 350 }

### 18) Delete the first item → netAmount follows
DELETE {{bill}}/InvoiceItems(02000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001)

### 19) Check
GET {{bill}}/Invoices({{manual}})?$select=invoiceNumber,netAmount,grossAmount

### 20) Issue it → ISSUED, dueDate = invoiceDate + 14
POST {{bill}}/Invoices({{manual}})/BillingService.issue
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### 21) Should FAIL 409: change an item of an issued invoice
PATCH {{bill}}/InvoiceItems(02000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000002)
Content-Type: application/json

{ "rate": 1 }